WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.950
Common Mistakes and Fixes.

2
00:00:02.230 --> 00:00:05.942
Day 15 of the Soft Skill Playbook course, in the English phase.

3
00:00:07.692 --> 00:00:08.716
The key idea.

4
00:00:08.996 --> 00:00:13.049
Today's goal: fix the mistakes that many Indian English speakers make.

5
00:00:13.329 --> 00:00:14.951
You'll recognise most of them.

6
00:00:15.231 --> 00:00:19.369
Fixing just these makes your English sound much clearer and more natural.

7
00:00:20.719 --> 00:00:21.573
Part 1.

8
00:00:21.853 --> 00:00:23.410
Articles: a, an, the.

9
00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:26.004
Here is a quick table:

10
00:00:26.284 --> 00:00:39.489
Rule, and Example. a before a consonant sound: a bank, a user, a university (sounds like you). an before a vowel sound: an app, an hour (silent h), an MBA (em). the when both people know which one:

11
00:00:39.769 --> 00:00:41.028
Please close the door.

12
00:00:41.308 --> 00:00:42.695
The meeting is at 3.

13
00:00:42.975 --> 00:00:45.940
No article for general plurals or uncountables:

14
00:00:46.220 --> 00:00:47.585
Developers like coffee.

15
00:00:47.865 --> 00:00:49.167
I need information.

16
00:00:49.447 --> 00:00:57.319
Places of routine (no the): go to work or school or bed or college. the for unique things: the sun, the internet, the CEO.

17
00:00:58.669 --> 00:01:01.741
I am going to office. then I'm going to the office.

18
00:01:02.021 --> 00:01:03.258
(or going to work).

19
00:01:04.608 --> 00:01:05.483
Part 2.

20
00:01:05.763 --> 00:01:06.787
Prepositions.

21
00:01:08.037 --> 00:01:09.381
Here is a quick table:

22
00:01:09.661 --> 00:01:30.802
Common mistake, and Correct. discuss about the plan: discuss the plan (no about). reach to office: reach the office or get to the office. married with her: married to her. good in English: good at English. angry on me: angry with me. wait for 5 minutes / wait me: wait for me. on the weekend or at the weekend: on Monday, in May, at 6 pm.

23
00:01:31.082 --> 00:01:32.149
He is in leave:

24
00:01:32.429 --> 00:01:33.389
He's on leave.

25
00:01:34.739 --> 00:01:36.403
I live here since 5 years:

26
00:01:36.683 --> 00:01:39.755
I've lived here for 5 years or since 2021.

27
00:01:41.105 --> 00:01:42.001
Part 3.

28
00:01:42.281 --> 00:01:43.518
Tenses and verbs.

29
00:01:44.768 --> 00:01:46.112
Here is a quick table:

30
00:01:46.392 --> 00:01:48.013
Mistake, and Fix, and Rule.

31
00:01:48.293 --> 00:01:49.659
I am having two kids.

32
00:01:49.939 --> 00:01:50.664
Fix:

33
00:01:50.944 --> 00:01:52.117
I have two kids.

34
00:01:52.397 --> 00:01:54.339
Rule: have for owning isn't -ing.

35
00:01:54.619 --> 00:01:55.728
I am knowing him.

36
00:01:56.008 --> 00:01:56.733
Fix:

37
00:01:57.013 --> 00:01:57.931
I know him.

38
00:01:58.211 --> 00:02:01.261
Rule: state verbs: know, understand, want, like.

39
00:02:01.541 --> 00:02:03.056
I have seen him yesterday.

40
00:02:03.336 --> 00:02:04.061
Fix:

41
00:02:04.341 --> 00:02:05.707
I saw him yesterday.

42
00:02:05.987 --> 00:02:08.141
Rule: finished time, then past simple.

43
00:02:08.421 --> 00:02:09.360
He don't know.

44
00:02:09.640 --> 00:02:10.365
Fix:

45
00:02:10.645 --> 00:02:11.627
He doesn't know.

46
00:02:11.907 --> 00:02:14.061
Rule: he or she or it, then doesn't.

47
00:02:14.341 --> 00:02:15.259
Did you went?

48
00:02:15.539 --> 00:02:16.264
Fix:

49
00:02:16.544 --> 00:02:17.461
Did you go?

50
00:02:17.741 --> 00:02:19.427
Rule: did + base verb.

51
00:02:19.707 --> 00:02:21.947
I am working here since 2020.

52
00:02:22.227 --> 00:02:22.952
Fix:

53
00:02:23.232 --> 00:02:25.493
I've been working here since 2020.

54
00:02:25.773 --> 00:02:28.269
Rule: since or for, then present perfect.

55
00:02:28.549 --> 00:02:29.701
Myself Ashish.

56
00:02:29.981 --> 00:02:30.707
Fix:

57
00:02:30.987 --> 00:02:33.312
I'm Ashish. / My name is Ashish.

58
00:02:33.592 --> 00:02:35.896
Rule: myself isn't used to introduce.

59
00:02:37.246 --> 00:02:38.163
Part 4.

60
00:02:38.443 --> 00:02:41.323
Indian English that confuses global listeners.

61
00:02:42.573 --> 00:02:43.917
Here is a quick table:

62
00:02:44.197 --> 00:02:45.307
Instead of, and Say.

63
00:02:45.587 --> 00:02:46.547
Do the needful:

64
00:02:46.827 --> 00:02:48.469
Could you please specific action?

65
00:02:48.749 --> 00:02:49.795
I have a doubt:

66
00:02:50.075 --> 00:02:51.291
I have a question.

67
00:02:51.571 --> 00:02:52.509
Revert back:

68
00:02:52.789 --> 00:02:54.368
Reply or Get back to me.

69
00:02:54.648 --> 00:02:55.501
Prepone:

70
00:02:55.781 --> 00:02:57.531
Move earlier or Bring forward.

71
00:02:57.811 --> 00:02:58.835
Out of station:

72
00:02:59.115 --> 00:03:00.587
Travelling or Out of town.

73
00:03:00.867 --> 00:03:02.595
Today itself or Now itself:

74
00:03:02.875 --> 00:03:04.133
Today or Right now.

75
00:03:04.413 --> 00:03:05.949
Pass out (from college):

76
00:03:06.229 --> 00:03:07.125
Graduate.

77
00:03:07.405 --> 00:03:08.344
Updation:

78
00:03:08.624 --> 00:03:09.435
Update.

79
00:03:10.785 --> 00:03:12.086
Kindly do it fast:

80
00:03:12.366 --> 00:03:13.838
Could you please do it soon?

81
00:03:14.118 --> 00:03:15.334
Only (at the end:

82
00:03:15.614 --> 00:03:16.873
I told you only):

83
00:03:17.153 --> 00:03:19.542
I told you. / I told you already.

84
00:03:19.822 --> 00:03:20.547
Is it?

85
00:03:20.827 --> 00:03:21.873
(as reaction):

86
00:03:22.153 --> 00:03:23.966
Really? / Oh, is that right?

87
00:03:25.316 --> 00:03:26.276
Part 5.

88
00:03:26.556 --> 00:03:28.177
Pronunciation hotspots.

89
00:03:29.427 --> 00:03:36.126
v and w: very (teeth on lip) versus west (round lips). th: think (tongue between teeth), not tink.

90
00:03:36.406 --> 00:03:37.195
Stress:

91
00:03:37.475 --> 00:03:42.190
DEVeloper, deVELop, COMpany, ANalyst, hoTEL, CALendar.

92
00:03:42.470 --> 00:03:47.889
Don't add a vowel before s + consonant: school not is-school, station not is-station.

93
00:03:49.239 --> 00:03:50.177
Part 6.

94
00:03:50.457 --> 00:03:52.420
Conversation: a quick self-check.

95
00:03:53.670 --> 00:03:55.697
Here is how the conversation goes.

96
00:03:55.977 --> 00:03:58.387
Did you discuss the release plan with the client?

97
00:03:58.667 --> 00:04:01.441
Yes, I discussed the plan with them this morning.

98
00:04:01.721 --> 00:04:03.150
And when is the release?

99
00:04:03.430 --> 00:04:06.459
They want to bring it forward by a week, to the 10th.

100
00:04:06.739 --> 00:04:07.443
Oh!

101
00:04:07.723 --> 00:04:09.110
Is Ravi available?

102
00:04:09.390 --> 00:04:10.819
I heard he's on leave.

103
00:04:12.169 --> 00:04:13.769
The conversation continues.

104
00:04:14.049 --> 00:04:17.847
He's on leave until Wednesday, but he'll reply to emails.

105
00:04:18.127 --> 00:04:19.236
Okay.

106
00:04:19.516 --> 00:04:22.396
I have a question about the test environment, actually.

107
00:04:22.676 --> 00:04:23.401
Sure.

108
00:04:23.681 --> 00:04:26.711
I've been working on it since Monday, so I can help.

109
00:04:28.061 --> 00:04:28.999
Part 7.

110
00:04:29.279 --> 00:04:30.197
Practice.

111
00:04:31.447 --> 00:04:32.769
Fix all the mistakes.

112
00:04:33.049 --> 00:04:36.377
Myself Priya, I am working in TCS since 4 years.

113
00:04:36.657 --> 00:04:39.601
Please do the needful and revert back today itself.

114
00:04:39.881 --> 00:04:42.463
I have a doubt, we can discuss about it tomorrow?

115
00:04:42.743 --> 00:04:45.516
He is in leave, he will reach to office on Monday.

116
00:04:45.796 --> 00:04:47.439
I am having an Honda bike.

117
00:04:48.789 --> 00:04:49.706
Success:

118
00:04:49.986 --> 00:04:50.839
Answers.

119
00:04:51.119 --> 00:04:51.994
I'm Priya.

120
00:04:52.274 --> 00:04:54.557
I've been working at TCS for four years.

121
00:04:54.837 --> 00:04:57.098
Could you please approve it and reply today?

122
00:04:57.378 --> 00:04:58.594
I have a question.

123
00:04:58.874 --> 00:05:00.346
Can we discuss it tomorrow?

124
00:05:00.626 --> 00:05:01.586
He's on leave.

125
00:05:01.866 --> 00:05:03.594
He'll get to the office on Monday.

126
00:05:03.874 --> 00:05:05.239
I have a Honda bike.

127
00:05:05.519 --> 00:05:07.546
(H in Honda is pronounced, so a).

128
00:05:08.896 --> 00:05:09.771
Part 8.

129
00:05:10.051 --> 00:05:11.096
Speak today.

130
00:05:12.346 --> 00:05:16.527
Choose 3 mistakes from this page that you make, and write them on a sticky note.

131
00:05:16.807 --> 00:05:19.687
Catch yourself once today and correct it out loud.

132
00:05:19.967 --> 00:05:21.333
Ask the AI tutor:

133
00:05:21.613 --> 00:05:24.258
Track my mistakes from this list in every lesson.

134
00:05:25.608 --> 00:05:26.525
Success:

135
00:05:26.805 --> 00:05:28.107
Phase 1 complete!.

136
00:05:28.387 --> 00:05:34.637
You can now build sentences, ask and answer any question, use the past and future, and speak politely.

137
00:05:34.917 --> 00:05:36.411
Tomorrow starts Phase 2:

138
00:05:36.691 --> 00:05:38.568
Communication and Confidence.

139
00:05:39.918 --> 00:05:41.454
That's the end of this lesson.

140
00:05:41.734 --> 00:05:46.385
Pick one script from it, say it out loud three times, and use it for real today.

141
00:05:46.665 --> 00:05:52.787
For extra practice, paste the Master Prompt into an AI assistant and role-play the conversation.

